// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: rule.stdlib.swap [Swap-Places] [Swap-Places-Conflict]; D-0235; conf.replace-passed-ref-beside-shared-reborrow
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// `replace(r, 9)` with `r` passed on whole while a shared reborrow `s` of
// `*r` lives: `replace` writes `*r` through `swap_places`, which takes
// `[Write]`'s premises (D-0235), so the call faults where `s` would
// otherwise have seen 9.
//
// D-0282: the static pass rejects this program before it runs (it was found
// at run time before): `replace` writes `*r` through argument 1 while `s`
// still borrows `*r`.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto r = &mut x;
    auto s = &*r;
    i32 old = replace(r, 9);
    printf("%v %v\n", *s, old);
}
